WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.280
A fictional customer opens the service chat.

2
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:34.760
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the customer: enters repair details.

3
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:45.880
The workflow offers available slots and waits for a choice.

4
00:00:45.880 --> 00:01:02.680
The booking workflow keeps the offered slots while it waits.

5
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:14.080
The same workflow waits with its offered slots.

6
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.480
Return to the same service conversation.

7
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:25.640
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the customer: selects B.

8
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:36.360
The same workflow books the chosen slot and confirms it in chat.

9
00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:54.600
The customer's choice resumes the waiting booking workflow.

10
00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:05.760
The workflow checks capacity before writing the booking.

11
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:18.120
Find this enquiry on DataIQ, iMBrace's records boards.

12
00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:24.700
The chosen slot becomes a booking on the demo calendar board.

13
00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:50.367
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the customer: requests twelve laptop setups.

14
00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:58.167
The workflow offers available fleet bays in the same chat.

15
00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:06.767
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the customer: chooses an offered bay.

16
00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:24.167
The fleet booking waits for the manager's decision.

17
00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:47.633
Open the workflow behind this fleet booking.

18
00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:59.633
The same workflow waits for the manager's decision.

19
00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:20.367
Find the fleet enquiry on the records board.

20
00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:25.033
The enquiry is waiting for its fleet booking decision.

21
00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:32.767
The booking version identifies the enquiry, customer, devices and chosen bay.

22
00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:51.700
Open the board for fleet booking decisions.

23
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:57.100
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the service manager: opens a decision.

24
00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:08.033
The decision names the enquiry and its exact booking version.

25
00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:17.233
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the service manager: records approval.

26
00:05:17.233 --> 00:05:38.567
Saving checks the booking version and resumes the waiting workflow.

27
00:05:38.567 --> 00:06:01.567
Return to the booking workflow after the decision.

28
00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:12.967
The workflow checks capacity and writes the approved booking.

29
00:06:12.967 --> 00:06:17.367
Return to the same service conversation.

30
00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:24.400
The approved fleet booking is confirmed in the same chat.
